WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.017
This example creates stay days in the CTE.

00:00:03.017 --> 00:00:06.622
Each CTE row represents one completed admission.

00:00:06.622 --> 00:00:12.292
The final query joins patients and calculates admission count and average stay per patient.

00:00:12.292 --> 00:00:15.592
The grain changes only in the final GROUP BY.

00:00:15.592 --> 00:00:19.502
That separation makes the transformation easier to validate.

00:00:19.502 --> 00:00:25.817
A CTE gives a name to an intermediate result so a complex query can be read in stages.

00:00:25.817 --> 00:00:33.257
Use it to clarify grain changes and major transformations, not simply to break every two lines into a new

00:00:33.257 --> 00:00:40.016
block. A useful CTE name describes what the rows represent, such as patient_totals or ranked_visits.
